  "consumed": "RAM Nugs Primary",
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost Per Dose:</strong> 150eb (Premium)</p>\n<p><em>This cocktail for corpo datafort dwellers leaked a while back, and now Dogtown cooks make gummies out of it. They aren’t tasty, but they’ll make you an unrelenting tank in the net. Just pretend you're eating pickled eggs... Unless that makes it worse.</em></p>\n<p><strong>⋙</strong> <strong>PRIMARY EFFECT</strong> <strong>⋘</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lasts 4 hours.</li>\n<li>For the duration of the Primary Effect, the user’s DEX and MOVE are reduced by 2 (Minimum 1).</li>\n<li>For the duration of the Primary Effect, all Net-sourced brain damage the user takes while Jacked In is reduced by 2.</li>\n<li>For the duration of the Primary Effect, once per Turn, the user may choose to take 2 points of Humanity Loss to attempt one additional Quickhack on a target they already attempted a Quickhack on during their Turn. This still requires spending the Net Action to Perform a Quickhack, and cannot be used to attempt the same Quickhack twice on the same target in a Turn.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>⋙</strong> <strong>SECONDARY EFFECT (DV17)</strong> <strong>⋘</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If the user wasn’t already addicted to RAM Nugs, they are now. While addicted, unless the user is experiencing the Primary Effect of RAM Nugs, the user’s TECH is reduced by 2 (Minimum 1).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 150eb (Premium) per dose<br>\n<strong>Type:</strong> Street Drug</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>While addicted, switch on the \"RAM Nugs Addiction\" effect.</li>\n<li>When an addicted character doses, use \"RAM Nugs Addicted Primary\" instead of the normal primary effect; it cancels the withdrawal penalties for the duration.</li>\n<li>Stat and skill changes are automated; caps, minimums, durations, and everything else are not.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Gear, Drugs, &amp; Frames &gt; Consumables &gt; Street Drugs).</em></p>"
  },
